menu "KVS WebRTC Configuration"

    config ENABLE_DATA_CHANNEL
        bool "Enable Data channel support using usrsctp"
        default y
        help
            Enables WebRTC Data channel support

    config USE_ESP_TLS_FOR_KVS
        bool "Use ESP-TLS for KVS TLS connections (TURN over TLS)"
        default y
        help
            Use ESP-TLS implementation instead of direct mbedTLS for TLS connections.
            This enables the use of ESP certificate bundle for CA verification,
            eliminating the need for certificate files on the filesystem.
            Recommended for ESP platforms to avoid certificate management complexity.

    config KVS_WEBRTC_ICE_TRANSPORT_RELAY_ONLY
        bool "Force ICE transport policy to RELAY only (use TURN exclusively)"
        default n
        help
            Force the ICE Agent to use TURN relay candidates only — host and
            srflx candidates are not advertised. This is required when the
            device is behind a one-way NAT that the remote peer cannot
            reach back into (e.g. qemu-xtensa user-mode networking / slirp,
            CGNAT on cellular). Both peers then connect through the AWS TURN
            relay, which only needs outbound connectivity from each side.

            Set this with `CONFIG_KVS_WEBRTC_ICE_TRANSPORT_RELAY_ONLY=y` in
            sdkconfig.defaults.qemu (or any deployment overlay where host
            candidates are unreachable from the remote peer's perspective).

            Default: n (ICE_TRANSPORT_POLICY_ALL — host + srflx + relay).
endmenu
